  <div class="notice warn small">Template: have these terms reviewed by a lawyer for the countries you sell to before going live. Text in [brackets] must be completed.</div>
  <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p><%= business.name %>, <%= business.address %>. Email: <%= business.email %>. VAT number: <%= business.vatId %>. <%= business.registration %>.</p>

  <h2>2. How a group deal works</h2>
  <p>Each deal has a price, a minimum number of buyers and a deadline (at most 30 days after the deal starts). When you join, you place an order for one unit at the stated price. That order only goes ahead if the deal reaches its minimum number of buyers by the deadline.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>If the minimum is reached by the deadline</strong>, your order becomes binding and we collect payment (see section 4). We confirm this by email.</li>
    <li><strong>If the minimum is not reached by the deadline</strong>, your order lapses. Nothing is charged and we remove your saved payment method.</li>
    <li>If you join after the minimum has already been reached, your order is binding as soon as you join and we collect payment straight away.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Prices</h2>
  <p>All prices are in euro (EUR) and include VAT. The price is the same in every EU country. The VAT inside it is calculated for your delivery country (using Stripe Tax) and shown before you save your payment method and on your receipt. [Delivery costs: state whether delivery is included in the price, or list delivery costs per country.]</p>

  <h2 id="payment">4. When payment is taken</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>When you join, you are not charged.</strong> Your payment method (card, or a SEPA Direct Debit mandate, which you can also set up through iDEAL) is saved securely by our payment provider Stripe. We never see or store your full card number or IBAN.</li>
    <li><strong>When the deal reaches its minimum</strong>, or immediately if you join after that, we charge the full price to your saved payment method and email you.</li>
    <li><strong>Cards</strong> are charged straight away. Your bank may ask you to confirm the payment (Strong Customer Authentication). If so, we email you a link to do that.</li>
    <li><strong>SEPA Direct Debit:</strong> by saving a SEPA mandate you authorise us (and Stripe, our payment service provider) to collect the deal price from your account once the deal reaches its minimum. Our "we're collecting payment now" email is your pre-notification of the amount and date. You agree that we may send it on the day we start the collection, instead of the standard 14 days before. The debit usually reaches your account within a few business days. Under the SEPA rules, you can ask your bank to refund an authorised debit within 8 weeks of the date it was taken.</li>
    <li><strong>If a payment fails</strong>, we may retry it automatically. We also email you a link to complete the payment, confirm it with your bank, or use another payment method. You have <strong>48 hours</strong> from our first collection attempt. If the payment still hasn't gone through after that, your order is cancelled and you owe us nothing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Delivery</h2>
  <p>[Expected delivery time after the deal closes, the countries you deliver to (EU only), and the carrier.] We order the goods once the 48-hour payment window has ended.</p>

  <h2 id="withdrawal">6. Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>If you are a consumer, you have the following right of withdrawal.</p>
  <h3>Right of withdrawal</h3>
  <p>You have the right to withdraw from this contract within 14 days without giving any reason. The withdrawal period will expire after 14 days from the day on which you acquire, or a third party other than the carrier and indicated by you acquires, physical possession of the goods.</p>
  <p>To exercise the right of withdrawal, you must inform us (<%= business.name %>, <%= business.address %>, <%= business.email %>) of your decision to withdraw from this contract by an unequivocal statement (e.g. a letter sent by post or an email). You may use the model withdrawal form below, but it is not obligatory.</p>
  <p>To meet the withdrawal deadline, it is sufficient for you to send your communication concerning your exercise of the right of withdrawal before the withdrawal period has expired.</p>
  <h3>Effects of withdrawal</h3>
  <p>If you withdraw from this contract, we shall reimburse to you all payments received from you, including the costs of delivery (with the exception of the supplementary costs resulting from your choice of a type of delivery other than the least expensive type of standard delivery offered by us), without undue delay and in any event not later than 14 days from the day on which we are informed about your decision to withdraw from this contract. We will carry out such reimbursement using the same means of payment as you used for the initial transaction, unless you have expressly agreed otherwise; in any event, you will not incur any fees as a result of such reimbursement.</p>
  <p>We may withhold reimbursement until we have received the goods back or you have supplied evidence of having sent back the goods, whichever is the earliest.</p>
  <p>You shall send back the goods or hand them over to us without undue delay and in any event not later than 14 days from the day on which you communicate your withdrawal from this contract to us. The deadline is met if you send back the goods before the period of 14 days has expired.</p>
  <p>[You will have to bear the direct cost of returning the goods. / We will bear the cost of returning the goods.]</p>
  <p>You are only liable for any diminished value of the goods resulting from the handling other than what is necessary to establish the nature, characteristics and functioning of the goods.</p>
  <h3>Before the deal goes ahead</h3>
  <p>You can also withdraw your order before the deal reaches its minimum, or before we have collected payment, by emailing <%= business.email %>. We then remove your saved payment method and do not charge you.</p>

  <h3>Model withdrawal form</h3>
  <div class="card small">
    <p>(Complete and return this form only if you wish to withdraw from the contract.)</p>
    <p>To <%= business.name %>, <%= business.address %>, <%= business.email %>:</p>
    <p>I/We (*) hereby give notice that I/We (*) withdraw from my/our (*) contract of sale of the following goods (*)/for the provision of the following service (*),</p>
    <p>Ordered on (*)/received on (*),<br>Name of consumer(s),<br>Address of consumer(s),<br>Signature of consumer(s) (only if this form is notified on paper),<br>Date</p>
    <p>(*) Delete as appropriate.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>7. Legal guarantee</h2>
  <p>You have the statutory rights for goods that are not in conformity with the contract (legal guarantee of at least two years from delivery under EU law). [Add any commercial guarantee.]</p>

  <h2>8. Complaints and applicable law</h2>
  <p>Contact us at <%= business.email %> with any complaint. [State whether you take part in alternative dispute resolution before a consumer arbitration body.] These terms are governed by the law of [country]. If you are a consumer, this does not take away the protection of the mandatory consumer law of the country where you live.</p>
